# v1.16 — QUEUED, DO NOT RUN YET. Restore ENDEX alongside the root's claim.
#
# Owner's decision, 2026-08-09, on assurance issue #31. Blocked on two things:
#   1. the code change below, which does not exist yet;
#   2. the v1.15 campaign (defend_brique_v12 / fireteam_defend_v17) being
#      scored, so the first-claim rule is measured before a second variable
#      lands on the same net.
#
# ── what #31 found ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# v1.14 gave DEFEND a horizon, which made it COMPLETABLE, which set
# `continuous_root = not is_completable(...)` to False — and that flag is the
# only gate on ENDEX. So horizon scenarios stopped announcing closure. Nobody
# decided that; it fell out of reusing one predicate for two purposes.
#
# The cost, measured independently at N=30 over seeds 500-529 against weights
# whose digests match our published checkpoint_sha256:
#
#   era              corpus                  success   announced on the net
#   v1.13 ENDEX      defend_brique_v9        27/30     27/27  and 27/27
#   v1.13 ENDEX      fireteam_defend_v15     25/30     25/25  and 24/24
#   v1.14 horizon    fireteam_defend_v16     30/30     0/27   and 0/30
#   v1.14 horizon    defend_brique_v11       30/30     1/30   and 23/29
#
# ENDEX announced 103 of 103 successes across four corpora. v1.14 announces 0
# of 57 on fireteam_defend. A policy that succeeds thirty times out of thirty
# and never once says the operation is over.
#
# ── why no reward lever fixes it ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# ENDEX is a PROTOCOL ACT: COMMAND emits it when the operation closes. Not
# optional, not learned, not trainable away — which is why it was 103/103.
# A root MISSION COMPLETE is an AGENT BEHAVIOUR: optional, priced, learnable in
# either direction. Identical prices produced 0.71-false spam on defend_brique
# and total silence on fireteam_defend.
#
# So v1.14 did not change the channel's rate, it changed its TYPE — from a
# guarantee of the protocol to a property of whatever the policy happened to
# learn. Pricing cannot restore a guarantee, only an average. The v1.15
# first-claim rule addresses the spam and leaves v16's 0/30 exactly where it is.
#
# ── the change ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Decouple the ENDEX gate from completability: COMMAND transmits ENDEX whenever
# it closes the operation, whether or not the root also claimed. A confirmed
# claim and an ENDEX are not redundant — the claim is a REPORT, the ENDEX is the
# FACT. Keep both.
#
# NOT rollout-neutral: it puts a message on the net, and traffic feeds the
# observation and the net arbitration. Hence the sequencing above; this is
# exactly the hazard #30 raised about the OPORD clause, and the reason #27 and
# #29 were run by hand rather than in parallel.
#
# Spaces stay frozen — this is emission, not vocabulary shape. Discrete(228)/Box(220).
#
# ── what to watch ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `successes_announced` — of the operations that succeeded, how many said so on
# the net. The v1.13 bar is 103/103. Anything short of complete on this axis is
# the finding, because it would mean the protocol act is still conditional on
# something it should not be.
#
# Also watch that restoring ENDEX does NOT suppress honest claiming: if the root
# stops reporting because COMMAND announces anyway, we have swapped one channel
# for the other again rather than holding both. Both arms carry the v1.15
# first-claim rule, so the claim economics are the ones already measured.
#
# ── controls: v11 / v16, NOT v12 / v17 ──────────────────────────────────────
# Corrected before launch. The v1.15 first-claim rule is REVERTED as of this
# cycle (owner's decision: it priced the first probe at -3.50 and bought total
# silence — 321 root claims -> 0, and P(DONE | a true claim is available) fell
# 0.401 -> 0.000083). So these arms run the PRE-v1.15 claim economics.
#
# That makes defend_brique_v11 / fireteam_defend_v16 the right controls: same
# reward economics, ENDEX off. Against v12 / v17 this would be a two-variable
# comparison — ENDEX restored AND the bonus rule reverted — which is exactly the
# confound the sequencing was built to avoid.
#
# The flag is stated explicitly even though it is now the default, so
# economics.json records it and the arm is self-documenting.
defend_brique_v13    --scenario defend_brique   --total-steps 3000000 --seed 12 --reward defend_survivor_scale=0.35 --reward root_done_bonus_first_claim_only=false
fireteam_defend_v18  --scenario fireteam_defend --total-steps 3500000 --seed 12 --reward defend_survivor_scale=0.35 --reward root_done_bonus_first_claim_only=false
